;; A macOS sandbox profile that denies every network operation and nothing
;; else. It is the stronger of the two profiles and the default statement
;; that the suite needs no network:
;;
;;   corepack pnpm test:denied
;;
;; which runs every package, and every file of `@cas/mcp-server` except the
;; one that cannot run here, under this profile. Only
;; `packages/mcp-server/src/redirect.stdio.test.ts` is excluded: it serves
;; real synthetic HTTP and HTTPS redirects from 127.0.0.1 to prove the
;; gateway refuses every one of them, so it needs a listening socket, which
;; this profile denies along with everything else. Nothing else is excluded,
;; and `src/coverage.test.ts` fails if anything else is added to the
;; exclusion.
;;
;; The denial is demonstrated to be active in the same session by a probe
;; under the same profile, which must reach no host off this machine:
;;
;;   sandbox-exec -f tools/offline-sandbox.sb node tools/sandbox-probe.mjs
;;
;; Under this profile the probe denies everything: a public IPv4 address, a
;; public IPv6 address, name resolution, a loopback socket, this host's own
;; non-loopback address, a UNIX-domain socket and a subprocess's connection.
;;
;; It denies UNIX-domain sockets too, so the PostgreSQL integration suite
;; cannot run under it. That is the point: the default suite must pass here
;; and `pnpm test:db` must not be able to.
;;
;; `tools/loopback-sandbox.sb` is the weaker profile that the one excluded
;; file runs under. It allows this machine's own addresses, not loopback
;; alone; read its header before relying on it.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network*)
